    "description": "Lightpath owns, builds, and operates metro and regional fiber networks serving enterprise, hyperscale, data center, wireless, and carrier customers. Its operating model is asset-heavy and network-based, centered on dark fiber, wavelength, Ethernet, and transport services delivered over owned fiber routes. Public materials describe approximately 10,800 unique route miles, more than 15,000 service locations, over 170 data centers, and eight cable landing stations on the network. The company began as Altice USA's fiber enterprise business and has since expanded into new metro markets including Boston, Miami, Northern Virginia, Phoenix, and Columbus. Altice USA agreed in July 2020 to sell a 49.99% interest in the business to Morgan Stanley Infrastructure Partners and closed the transaction in December 2020, while retaining a 50.01% interest. Public disclosures reviewed through late 2024 continued to describe this 50.01% Altice and 49.99% MSIP ownership structure.",
